0007B9r 2               ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0007B9r 2               ; DrawLeftTriangle / DrawRightTriangle — a small 3x5 "you can go this way"
0007B9r 2               ; affordance, the same design language as DrawUpTriangle/DrawDownTriangle
0007B9r 2               ; (a solid filled arrowhead coming to a single-pixel point, not the font's
0007B9r 2               ; thin </> glyphs) rotated 90 degrees, for a left/right control -- the
0007B9r 2               ; color swatches. DrawTitleScreen centers this against an 8x8 swatch
0007B9r 2               ; (even height, so a perfect pixel-exact center isn't possible against a
0007B9r 2               ; 5-tall odd shape -- it lands within half a pixel, which reads as
0007B9r 2               ; centered) rather than trying to size the triangle to match the swatch
0007B9r 2               ; 1-for-1, which is what previously flattened its point into an edge.
0007B9r 2               ; In: A = top row, X = left col, Y = color
0007B9r 2               ; Out: none
0007B9r 2               ; Clobbers: A, X, Y, SCAN_TMP, SCAN_TMP2, TEXT_COLOR, plus everything
0007B9r 2               ;   PixelSet clobbers
0007B9r 2               ; -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
0007B9r 2               DrawLeftTriangle:
